@@ -86,9 +86,14 @@ STRPM|v2|msg=<id>|seq=<n>|channel=<channel>|target=<target>|flags=<n>|part=<i>|p
 The relay appends authenticated sender metadata derived from the STR server session:
 
 ```text
-|sender=<connectionId>|senderName=<name>|serverTick=<tick>
+|sender=<connectionId>|senderPlayerId=<playerId>|senderName=<name>|serverTick=<tick>
 ```
 
+These four names are reserved. The relay rejects an envelope that already carries one,
+and the bridge reads them from the tail of the envelope: the head is written by the peer
+and the tail is written by the relay, so a reader that takes the first match would take
+the peer's copy. Nothing in the peer-written head may reuse a reserved name.
+
 Targets supported by the scripting relay are:
 
 - `all`
